    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **269 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change computes owner initials and returns them in the owner response as the `initials` field.\n\nSince the owner responses (both create and get) go through MapStruct's `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, I implemented `initials` as a derived field there \u2014 mirroring the existing `displayName` derivation, so it's available on every owner response consistently:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression computing initials from the first letters of first + last name, upper-cased and dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" +\n   owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nFor \"John\" / \"Sur\u2026\", this yields `\"J.S.\"` as required. The new `Cp07Tests.coreInitials` passes, and the full suite (269 tests) remains green.",
